    "explanation": "At $B$ the angle between the two legs is $235^\\circ - 160^\\circ = 75^\\circ$. The cosine rule gives $HJ \\approx 13.8$ km, the sine rule gives angle $BHJ \\approx 39.2^\\circ$, and since $J$ is clockwise from $B$ as seen from $H$, its bearing is $055^\\circ + 39.2^\\circ = 094.2^\\circ$.",
    "workedSolution": "**(a)** $75^\\circ$.\n\n**(b)** $\\sqrt{189.44} = 13.8$ km.\n\n**(c)** $\\sin^{-1}(0.6316) = 39.2^\\circ$.\n\n**(d)** $094.2^\\circ$.",
